                                "sense_id": "39105663-1ae1-36fc-aba9-42276f80de69",
                                "text": "A Pair of Plates consisted of the breast and back, each formed of three or more pieces; Gyders were straps to draw together the open parts; the Haustement, a stiff under garment to keep the body straight and erect; the Rerebrace ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2fe182f-843b-4bd6-9431-9d626190eb6a",
                                "sense_id": "39105663-1ae1-36fc-aba9-42276f80de69",
                                "text": "A maniple, i.e. many folds, a name for the haustement worn in the time of Hen. VI under the armour."
                            },
